{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ViT-L, avgpool, concat → 62.9% acc, 4.54 GPU hrs), the most critical uncertainty is whether the RNA modality actually adds meaningful value over image-only. Config_009 (image_only, multiprofile, ViT-L, avgpool) is a clean ablation that removes only the RNA branch while keeping the image encoder (ViT-L), profile setting (multiprofile), and aggregation (avgpool) identical to config_001. If image-only approaches ~62%, we can redirect remaining budget toward cheaper image-centric or single-modality configurations. If it falls well below, multimodal fusion is confirmed essential and we should invest in stronger RNA encoders (scGPT, scVI) and fusion strategies. Expected relative cost: moderate (~3–3.5 GPU hrs), cheaper than config_001 since there is no RNA encoding or cross-modal fusion, but still uses the expensive ViT-L backbone. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the core architectural choice (multimodal vs. unimodal) before committing remaining budget to specific encoder/fusion variants."
}

